('The tendency to form catenated compounds (chains) is highest for', 'Nitrogen', 'Silicon', 'Carbon', 'Oxygen', 'option3', 'C-C bond is very strong ($347\;\text{kJ/mol}$). Carbon forms extensive chains, rings, and networks. Si-Si is weaker.', 'c_p_block_general', 2, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
