('The basicity (number of replaceable H atoms) of H$_3$PO$_3$ (phosphorous acid) is', '$3$', '$2$', '$1$', '$0$', 'option2', 'H$_3$PO$_3$: 2 P-OH bonds + 1 P-H bond (non-acidic) + 1 P=O. Only 2 replaceable H atoms. Dibasic.', 'c_p_block_general', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
('Sulphuric acid acts as a dehydrating agent because', 'It has a strong affinity for water and can remove H and OH from compounds', 'It is a weak acid', 'It is volatile', 'It is a reducing agent', 'option1', 'Conc. H$_2$SO$_4$ dehydrates sugar (C$_{12}$H$_{22}$O$_{11} \to$ 12C + 11H$_2$O), formic acid (HCOOH $\to$ CO + H$_2$O), etc.', 'c_p_block_general', 3, 'JEE Mains Prep', 'approved'),
